<speak>We can note that later afternoon is your usual preference and check your availability when arranging a future call. An appointment request can make clear that it is a telephone conversation, so you don't have to wonder whether you're expected to attend in person. If your week is especially busy, you can suggest a different window when we contact you. For scheduling, you don't need to explain all your business commitments; a simple indication that a proposed time doesn't suit you is enough.</speak>